    "body": "<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-requirements\">\n<p>You must have a paid Klaviyo account to use this feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p>Learn how to use the Email AI tool to create an AI-generated campaign email. The option to draft content with AI accepts natural language inputs (i.e., normal phrases and sentences) and generates an email based on a reference template.</p>\n<p>The AI-generated email can be sent as-is or provide a starting point from which you can edit the content yourself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JC1B507XVA72C9FN8ZP06DPS\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>This article covers the AI generation option when creating campaigns. If this is your first time creating a campaign, learn <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005054847\">how to create and send an email campaign</a>, or if you’d like to know how to create a campaign email without using AI, learn <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/4407911841435\">how to use the email template editor</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JC1B507YFQ53BNTJXP1NWFNB\">Use AI to draft a campaign email</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Navigate to the <em>Campaigns</em> tab and do one of the following:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Click <strong>Create campaign </strong>for a new campaign. </li>\n<li>Click the action button and select <strong>Edit campaign</strong> to edit an existing campaign.</li>\n<li>Click the action button and select <strong>Clone</strong> to copy an existing campaign.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>After choosing the lists or segments you want to send to in the <em>Audience</em> step, click <strong>Next</strong>.</li>\n<li>Choose a drag-and-drop template for your email.<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>You must have a drag-and-drop template selected for the “Draft email content” option to appear.</li>\n<li>For the best results, choose a pre-built template from the library or one you have already created that contains content (e.g., text blocks, buttons, splits, tables, etc). This gives Email AI a better idea of the structure and style you are looking for. Templates that consist primarily of images are more difficult to draft using Email AI.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>In the template preview modal, choose <strong>Draft email content.</strong><br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30538483583003\" alt=\"\" width=\"550\" height=\"526\">\n</li>\n<li>In the text field under <em>Describe your email content</em>, describe what you want to change over the reference template. If you aren’t exactly sure how to write a prompt, select 1 of the examples that appears below the text field.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30538513016987\" alt=\"\">\n</li>\n<li>Once you set up the description and settings, click <strong>Generate drafts</strong>.<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>This creates 3 drafts for you to choose from.</li>\n<li>It may take a few seconds before the drafts are fully generated.</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>In the <em>Preview</em> section, click on the reference email or 1 of the 3 drafts to preview it in the window on the right.<br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/30538483593499\" alt=\"\" width=\"351\" height=\"439\">\n</li>\n<li>You have 2 options, either edit the content yourself or generate more drafts:</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>If one of the drafts is close to what you want, select it and click <strong>Open in editor</strong> in the top right to enter the email template editor. Edit the generated content as desired. </li>\n<li>If you want to try again, revise your description and click <strong>Generate drafts </strong>again.<br>\n<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n<p>If you’d like to use AI tools to further enhance your email within the email template editor, learn <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/21977834205723\">how to use Email AI to generate email content</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01JC1B507YEBXHV6RYXNNF83YH\">Prompt best practices</h2>\n<p>To get the best results possible from the draft generation, provide as much context and specificity as you can on what you are looking for within the 500 character limit.</p>\n<p>Examples of context and specificity:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Specific sales: “20% off” or “everything half off sale.”</li>\n<li>Context about your brand: “for my makeup brand” or “for a sale on T-shirts.”</li>\n<li>Language or tone: “use a professional tone” or “use “Gen Z energy.”</li>\n</ul>",
    "user_segment_ids": []
  },
